    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: fiscal-year basis for date-derived values\n\nThe fiscal year starts **1 July** and is named by its starting calendar year (a date on/after 1 July belongs to that year, earlier dates to the previous one).\n\n**Files touched (4):**\n\n1. **New `util/FiscalYear.java`** \u2014 a small, cohesive helper with two trivial static methods (`of` and `label`). All fiscal-year logic lives here rather than being spread through existing classes, so no existing method grew in complexity.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` mapping (`FiscalYear.label(registrationDate)` \u2192 `\"FY<YY>\"`) and switched `membershipNumber`'s year segment from the calendar year to the fiscal year via `FiscalYear.of(...)`. The registration date passed in is already business-day-adjusted by `defaultRegistrationDate`.\n\n3. **`util/Membership.java`** \u2014 replaced the 365-day tenure check with an elapsed-fiscal-years check (`FiscalYear.of(now) - FiscalYear.of(registrationDate) > 1`), dropping the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import and updating the doc.\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field) and updated the `membershipNumber` description to note YY is the fiscal year.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** the new behaviour is isolated in a fresh low-complexity class, so the biggest cost lever (`WMC_other`) stayed tiny \u2014 the edits to `Membership.points` and the mapper each changed only one or two lines and touched no complex surrounding methods.\n\n**Tests:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsFiscalYear` (asserting `fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
